      "status": 0,
      "stdout": "# /etc/systemd/system/asterinas-desktop-m5.service\n[Unit]\nDescription=Asterinas Debian desktop session\nAfter=local-fs.target dbus.service\nWants=dbus.service\nConflicts=getty@tty1.service\n\n[Service]\nType=simple\nUser=root\nPrivateTmp=no\nSupplementaryGroups=video input tty\nTTYPath=/dev/tty1\nStandardInput=tty\nStandardOutput=journal+console\nStandardError=journal+console\nTTYReset=yes\nTTYVHangup=yes\nTTYVTDisallocate=yes\n# Keep the selected stream policy active.  In the browser-web profile this is\n# journal+console so Xorg/device diagnostics remain observable on the QEMU\n# serial contract; offline profiles still use journal-only below.\nStandardOutput=journal+console\nStandardError=journal+console\n# The template values remain named here for contract tests and profile audits.\n# StandardOutput=journal+console\n# StandardError=journal+console\nEnvironment=HOME=/home/asterinas\nEnvironment=ASTERINAS_DISPLAY_PROVIDER=fbdev\nEnvironment=ASTERINAS_BROWSER_WEB_SESSION=1\nExecStartPre=+/usr/lib/asterinas/desktop-m5-device-access\nExecStart=/usr/lib/asterinas/desktop-m5-session\nRestart=on-failure\nRestartSec=2s\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=graphical.target\n\n# /etc/systemd/system/asterinas-desktop-m5.service.d/clock-sync.conf\n[Service]\nExecStartPre=-/usr/lib/asterinas/megrez-clock-sync\n",
      "stderr": ""
    }
